    char_literal_lexer_switch_staged_2026-11-03, P2, open, "Staged lexer switch: single-quoted 'x' becomes char-only (ADR-005, user decision 2026-11-03); multi-scalar legacy '...' raw strings move to r\"...\". Blocked on the stage3 self-build passing (frozen stage2 compiles the compiler lexer). Source migration tool + per-dir token-neutral batches land first; guard scripts/check/check-no-single-quoted-raw-string.shs is advisory now, blocking after the switch, and every staged warning (incl. new raw strings, char-as-i64, char-vs-text, non-exhaustive match) becomes an ERROR once Windows, macOS and Linux all have a working self-hosted Simple binary (promotion trigger)", doc/08_tracking/bug/char_literal_lexer_switch_staged_2026-11-03.md, 0, "ADR-005 char literal syntax and migration plan", 2026-11-03, 2026-11-10, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    char_literal_lexer_switch_staged_2026-11-03, 0, "2026-11-10 P2 lane (release/1.0.0). Pending stage re-checked: activation step 2 (bootstrap lane records a passing stage3 self-build) is still unmet on every platform, so steps 3-5 (migration batches, default flip, blocking guard) stay blocked; status stays open. Parity defect fixed inside the gated path: pure-Simple scan_char_literal rejected '\\x41', '\\x7', '\\101', '\\7' as invalid escapes while the seed (scan_char_literal -> process_escape) and the pure-Simple double-quoted scanner both decode them, so the two front ends disagreed under SIMPLE_CHAR_LITERAL_LEXER=1 and '\\x41' != \"\\x41\" inside pure Simple. Fix: src/compiler/10.frontend/core/lexer_struct.spl scan_char_literal now decodes \\xNN (1-2 hex digits, 0 digits is a lex error) and \\N..\\NNN octal (covers \\0) with the same rule as scan_string. Spec: test/01_unit/compiler/frontend/lexer_char_literal_gate_spec.spl, 2 new examples (hex/octal escapes; char-vs-string escape parity over 8 escapes) + 3 new error cases; red 5/7 -> green 7/7; parser_char_literal_gate_spec 5/5, lexer_indentation_eof_emits_token_spec 6/6, lexer_reference_tokens_v1_spec 3/3, lexer_byte_spans_spec 4/4 unchanged. Next stage (seed side, needs a cargo build so it is NOT done here): the seed char scanner also accepts forms the pure-Simple string scanner does not (\\a \\b \\f \\v, bare \\uXXXX, \\: \\/ \\. \\-, and unknown \\q -> q); the seed must narrow to the shared set (n t r \\\\ \\' \\\" \\xNN octal \\u{...}) in the one-PR switch of activation step 4 so both lexers reject the same literals."
